---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Code of Conduct"
  description="The standards we expect at every Edmonton Data Society event and in our online spaces."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-4xl">Code of Conduct</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-stone-500">
      Draft — organizers should review and adopt this before launch.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-6">
      <p>
        Edmonton Data Society is a community for everyone. We expect all participants — attendees,
        speakers, sponsors, and organizers — to help keep it that way, at events and in our online
        spaces.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl">Expected behaviour</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
        <li>Be respectful of differing viewpoints, experience levels, and backgrounds.</li>
        <li>Assume good faith and give people room to ask beginner questions.</li>
        <li>Respect people's time, attention, and consent — including for photos.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-2xl">Unacceptable behaviour</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
        <li>
          Harassment or discrimination based on gender, gender identity or expression, sexual
          orientation, disability, physical appearance, race, ethnicity, age, religion, or any other
          protected ground.
        </li>
        <li>Deliberate intimidation, stalking, or unwelcome sexual attention.</li>
        <li>Sustained disruption of talks or other events.</li>
        <li>Unsolicited recruiting or sales pitches to individuals who have not invited them.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-2xl">Reporting</h2>
      <p>
        If you experience or witness a violation, contact an organizer in person, message a
        moderator on Discord, or email <a
          href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}
          class="text-accent underline underline-offset-4">{SITE.email}</a
        >. Reports are handled confidentially.
      </p>
      <p>
        Organizers may take any action they consider appropriate, including a warning or removal
        from the event and community spaces without refund.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
